  <h2>Caveats</h2>
  <table>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <th>Permissions</th>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Do not depend upon the auto-grant status of permissions. <b>Always</b> use the <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Run_time_permissions" target="_blank">run_time_permissions</a> event.
If the script lacks the permission <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/PERMISSION_TRACK_CAMERA" target="_blank">PERMISSION_TRACK_CAMERA</a>, the script will shout an error on <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/DEBUG_CHANNEL" target="_blank">DEBUG_CHANNEL</a> and the operation fails (but the script continues to run).
Once the <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/PERMISSION_TRACK_CAMERA" target="_blank">PERMISSION_TRACK_CAMERA</a> permission is granted there is no way to revoke it except from inside the script (for example, with a new <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlRequestPermissions" target="_blank">llRequestPermissions</a> call) or the script is reset or deleted.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Returns zero when permissions have not been granted.</p>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`-- say the camera aspect ratio and field of view (FOV)
local has_perms = false
function LLEvents.on_rez(a)
    ll.ResetScript()
end
local function main()
    ll.RequestPermissions(ll.GetOwner(), PERMISSION_TRACK_CAMERA)
end
function LLEvents.run_time_permissions(permission)
    has_perms = (permission == PERMISSION_TRACK_CAMERA)
end
function LLEvents.touch_start(events)
    local num_touches = #events
    if has_perms then
        local aspect = ll.GetCameraAspect()
        local fov = ll.GetCameraFOV()
        ll.OwnerSay("aspect = " .. tostring(aspect) .. "  FOV = " .. tostring(fov))
    else
        ll.RequestPermissions(ll.GetOwner(), PERMISSION_TRACK_CAMERA)
    end
end

main()
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`// say the camera aspect ratio and field of view (FOV)
integer has_perms = FALSE;
default
{
    on_rez(integer a)
    {
        llResetScript();
    }
    state_entry()
    {
        llRequestPermissions(llGetOwner(), PERMISSION_TRACK_CAMERA);
    }
    run_time_permissions(integer permission)
    {
        has_perms = (permission == PERMISSION_TRACK_CAMERA);
    }
    touch_start(integer num_touches)
    {
        if (has_perms)
        {
            float aspect = llGetCameraAspect();
            float fov = llGetCameraFOV();
            llOwnerSay("aspect = " + (string)aspect + "  FOV = " + (string)fov);
        }
        else
        {
            llRequestPermissions(llGetOwner(), PERMISSION_TRACK_CAMERA);
        }
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`-- Scale an object to fit the aspect ratio of the viewer.
local function fit_to_screen()
    -- The X axis from the left to  the right edge of the screen is 0.0 to width value.
    -- The Y axis is always 1.
    local x = ll.GetCameraAspect()
    local y = 1
    ll.SetLinkPrimitiveParamsFast(LINK_THIS, {PRIM_SIZE, vector(0, x, y)})
end
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`// Scale an object to fit the aspect ratio of the viewer.
fit_to_screen()
{
    // The X axis from the left to  the right edge of the screen is 0.0 to width value.
    // The Y axis is always 1.
    float x = llGetCameraAspect();
    float y = 1;
    llSetLinkPrimitiveParamsFast(LINK_THIS, [PRIM_SIZE, <0, x, y>]);
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <p>The reported aspect ratio is based on values provided by the viewer to the simulator. This may cause visual oddities if there&#39;s a discrepancy between the viewer&#39;s reported camera and what the viewer actually displays to the user. For example: entering mouselook may cause portions of the viewer interface to disappear, which alters the amount of space available to the HUD, which can lead to misaligned positioning or slightly-off aspect ratio. (This is currently considered a viewer-bug.)</p>
